From c83d32c47514c5579b8f456e52cafa1704b21365 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 03:19:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00911/11171] [outer-loop] decouple RFT harness from base model
 via GeneratorSpec

Operator concern: don't tie the project to MiniCPM5-1B. The generator is the swappable
commodity part (decentralization rule 1 / hybrid architecture); the verifier is the
product. The MiniCPM-specific generation quirks (stop on <|im_end|> + </s>;
enable_thinking=False) were duplicated inline in two scripts.

generator_spec.py: GeneratorSpec(model_id, enable_thinking, extra_stop_tokens, templates)
with resolve_stop_ids(tok) + format_prompt(tok, q); KNOWN_SPECS + for_model() factory
(unlisted models get a safe default). Swapping base model = change MODEL_ID.

Wired both phase1 (eval) and onpolicy (generation) to use it. Behavior-preserving:
verified MiniCPM resolves to the identical stop_ids [1, 130073] as the old hardcoded
logic; unlisted model swaps to default; both scripts import clean. Running #1 unaffected
(modules already loaded in memory; refactor applies to future runs). NOTE: transformers
path only; SOTA *-GGUF repos load via llama.cpp (separate, per CLAUDE.md GGUF rule).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
